WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:33.050 --> 00:00:39.829
I think of all the stories that we've investigated
so far, all the fundamental myths of creation

00:00:39.829 --> 00:00:44.290
that we've investigated so far, the two that
we're going to talk about in detail today

00:00:44.290 --> 00:00:48.850
are probably the two stories that have had
more impact on the course of world history

00:00:48.850 --> 00:00:50.470
than any other two.

00:00:50.470 --> 00:00:54.871
I'm going to talk in some detail today about
the story of creation laid out in Genesis

00:00:54.871 --> 00:00:58.940
and also the story of the Buddha's enlightenment.

00:00:58.940 --> 00:01:04.100
Both stories are also characterized by a kind
of depth that's virtually elimitless.

00:01:04.100 --> 00:01:10.110
And I think in some ways that the topics we're
going to discuss today are the most enlightening

00:01:10.110 --> 00:01:19.710
of all the many ideas that we've traveled
through so far in this series.

00:01:19.710 --> 00:01:26.460
So, we're gonna be concentrating on an analysis
of this schema again.

00:01:26.460 --> 00:01:31.030
The idea being here of course that the world
of experience, which is the world that mythology

00:01:31.030 --> 00:01:37.800
is attempting to describe has these fundamental
constituent elements, one associated with

00:01:37.800 --> 00:01:45.300
chaos or nature or the unknown, one associated
with culture or the great father or the predictable.

00:01:45.300 --> 00:01:52.110
And another associated with the archetypical
son, the individual who's the offspring of

00:01:52.110 --> 00:01:57.979
the interplay of these two fundamental forces
But given that part of the purpose of this

00:01:57.979 --> 00:02:04.250
series is to elucidate the causes of war and
motivation for war, attention paid to the

00:02:04.250 --> 00:02:08.220
dualistic nature of the individual is of,
of paramount importance.

00:02:08.220 --> 00:02:12.810
So we could say that just as nature has it's
terrible side and just as culture has its

00:02:12.810 --> 00:02:17.140
terrible side, so the individual has his or
her terrible side.

00:02:17.140 --> 00:02:24.690
And the depth of that, capacity say for atrocity
and vengefulness is just as deep as the depth

00:02:24.690 --> 00:02:27.780
of terror that the unknown itself holds.

00:02:27.780 --> 00:02:35.550
I think this is a difficult, a difficult fact
for normal individuals to grasp, given that

00:02:35.550 --> 00:02:40.879
we're highly motivated to view ourselves as,
if not precisely good, at least as relatively

00:02:40.879 --> 00:02:41.879
harmless.

00:02:41.879 --> 00:02:47.000
But the evidence that as individuals we are
relatively harmless is very, very thin indeed.

00:02:47.000 --> 00:02:56.000
And I don't think it's possible to understand
the depth of motivation for atrocity and social

00:02:56.000 --> 00:02:59.780
conflict without coming to terms with the
capacity for evil that's characteristic of

00:02:59.780 --> 00:03:00.780
the individual.

00:03:00.780 --> 00:03:05.720
Now both the story in Genesis and the story
of the Buddha's enlightenment, lay bare in

00:03:05.720 --> 00:03:09.320
many ways the nature of the structure of individual
evil.

00:03:09.320 --> 00:03:11.770
And also not only it's structure, but its
motivation.

00:03:11.770 --> 00:03:18.680
Why it is that people would turn more or less
voluntarily away from the good and embrace

00:03:18.680 --> 00:03:21.790
what can only be described as it's polar opposite.

00:03:21.790 --> 00:03:28.720
So in addition to making reference to this
structural schema of course, we're also going

00:03:28.720 --> 00:03:37.160
to be discussing it's, the typical mode of
interaction of these elements of experience.

00:03:37.160 --> 00:03:43.050
You may note for example that this diagram
with which you're now very familiar, the notion

00:03:43.050 --> 00:03:47.851
of order, chaos and reestablishment of order
also parallels the structure of the story

00:03:47.851 --> 00:03:52.690
in Genesis, the creation where human beings
are created first and exist in a paradisal

00:03:52.690 --> 00:03:53.690
state.

00:03:53.690 --> 00:04:01.210
That that paradise is disrupted as, as a consequence
of some, some event of virtually cosmic significance,

00:04:01.210 --> 00:04:06.680
that as a consequence of that disruption people
are destined to live a profane existence in

00:04:06.680 --> 00:04:18.690
constant wait for the next state of order.

00:04:18.690 --> 00:04:23.630
So just as this is a fundamental archetypical
structure so that fundamental archetypical

00:04:23.630 --> 00:04:28.060
structure is, constitutes the, the basic grammar
for this story in Genesis.

00:04:28.060 --> 00:04:35.199
Now what we're gonna do to begin with is to
describe precisely how this idea of paradise,

00:04:35.199 --> 00:04:40.590
descent and the search for paradise is illustrated
symbolically in Genesis and exactly what those

00:04:40.590 --> 00:04:42.460
symbolic representations mean.

00:04:42.460 --> 00:04:46.680
The idea here being that the reason that the
authors of Genesis, the multiple authors of

00:04:46.680 --> 00:04:52.270
Genesis extending over thousands and thousands
of years chose those symbols as not because

00:04:52.270 --> 00:04:58.249
they were labouring to be obscure or not because
they were establishing a pre-empirical representation

00:04:58.249 --> 00:05:04.849
of reality, a kind of quasi scientific representation,
but because these symbols have an elusive

00:05:04.849 --> 00:05:10.370
or metaphorical richness that enables a story,
although short to be characterized by an almost

00:05:10.370 --> 00:05:11.629
infinite depth.

00:05:11.629 --> 00:05:12.629
That's part of the reason.

00:05:12.629 --> 00:05:17.330
The other part of the reason is that when
you say something profound, you say it using

00:05:17.330 --> 00:05:20.669
the language, the clearest language that you
have access to.

00:05:20.669 --> 00:05:26.650
And if the story is almost unutterably profound,
then the images in which it is enshrouded

00:05:26.650 --> 00:05:30.270
are almost incomprehensibly complex.

00:05:30.270 --> 00:05:37.521
It has to be that way because if the target
of the investigation is reality itself, something

00:05:37.521 --> 00:05:43.409
so complex that we cannot conceptualize it
fully, then the language that we use to represent

00:05:43.409 --> 00:05:47.099
that reality has to stretch us to the limits
of our ability to understand

00:05:47.099 --> 00:05:53.199
and it is the case that the story in Genesis
say as much as the stories of Buddhist enlightenment

00:05:53.199 --> 00:05:58.840
constitutes an artistic endeavor on the part
of the human race to portray the nature of

00:05:58.840 --> 00:06:05.229
human reality and to explain the behavioural
and philosophical consequences of that reality.

00:06:05.229 --> 00:06:10.539
That being a tall order perhaps we should
forgive the multiple authors for only being

00:06:10.539 --> 00:06:16.380
able to manage it in a way that's essentially
imagistic and dramatic, rather than explicit,

00:06:16.380 --> 00:06:20.279
logical, philosophical and fully developed.

00:06:20.279 --> 00:06:26.910
So the first thing I'd like to point out to
you is to, is a statement made by Eliade,

00:06:26.910 --> 00:06:30.490
which I think is one of the most enlightening
things I ever read.

00:06:30.490 --> 00:06:35.930
Now, the first thing that Eliade does is describe
the universality of flood mythology.

00:06:35.930 --> 00:06:37.900
But then he puts a twist on it.

00:06:37.900 --> 00:06:46.159
So the idea behind flood mythology is something
like this, if societies deviate from an emergent,

00:06:46.159 --> 00:06:50.689
a necessarily emergent kind of morality, a
kind of morality that takes the viewpoint

00:06:50.689 --> 00:06:55.029
of all the inhabitants of a given society
into account, if a society deviates from that

00:06:55.029 --> 00:06:58.780
viewpoint sufficiently, it dooms itself to
annihilation.

00:06:58.780 --> 00:07:05.569
That annihilation being represented mythologically
as the flooding of the society by the precosmogonic

00:07:05.569 --> 00:07:08.629
waters, the primordial element or chaos.

00:07:08.629 --> 00:07:14.969
So societies that are tyrannical doom themselves
to eradication by chaos, a simple equation.

00:07:14.969 --> 00:07:20.740
But made more complicated by Eliade, his observation
that more than one factor plays a role in

00:07:20.740 --> 00:07:22.119
the establishment of the tyranny.

00:07:22.119 --> 00:07:27.560
On the one hand there's straight degeneration
of cultural presuppositions in that if you

00:07:27.560 --> 00:07:34.210
establish a state or a game, which has particular
rules, because the environment is constantly

00:07:34.210 --> 00:07:38.300
transforming itself, the rules by necessity
become out of date.

00:07:38.300 --> 00:07:43.509
So merely as a consequence of the progression
of time, the presuppositions on which any

00:07:43.509 --> 00:07:48.009
state are founded tend to become less and
less relevant to the current environment.

00:07:48.009 --> 00:07:49.009
Okay.

00:07:49.009 --> 00:07:53.339
So there’s this aging and senility merely
as a consequence of thermodynamic processes.

00:07:53.339 --> 00:07:57.909
But then Iliad also points out that there's
one additional factor which has to be attributed,

00:07:57.909 --> 00:08:03.719
not to society, but to the individuals that
make up that society, which is that the strictures

00:08:03.719 --> 00:08:10.830
and rules on which society was founded can
be constantly and carefully updated when necessary,

00:08:10.830 --> 00:08:16.120
If all the individuals that make up that society
are perfectly willing to confront exemplars

00:08:16.120 --> 00:08:21.289
of emerging chaos in their own lives when
those exemplars emerge, which is to say that

00:08:21.289 --> 00:08:25.419
it's perfectly reasonable to be guided in
your personality by the structures of your

00:08:25.419 --> 00:08:26.419
state.

00:08:26.419 --> 00:08:30.199
But if you face something unknown that those
rules cannot handle, it's a moral necessity

00:08:30.199 --> 00:08:36.560
and obligation on your part to face that emergent
anomaly forthrightly to solve it if you can,

00:08:36.560 --> 00:08:40.440
and then to communicate the consequences of
your solution to the rest of the members of

00:08:40.440 --> 00:08:41.440
your society.

00:08:41.440 --> 00:08:47.680
Now what Eliade points out is that the individual
who, who removes him or her self from the

00:08:47.680 --> 00:08:54.320
responsibility of confronting their own anomaly
speeds the process by which the state decays.

00:08:54.320 --> 00:09:00.060
So the decay of the state and the possibility
for the emergence of chaos is an interaction

00:09:00.060 --> 00:09:03.100
between the tenancy of the state to disorder,
the tendency of the state to, archaism and

00:09:03.100 --> 00:09:09.220
senility merely as a consequence of change
and the voluntarily the voluntary unwillingness

00:09:09.220 --> 00:09:13.759
of the citizens that comprise that state to
face the unknown courageously when it confronts

00:09:13.759 --> 00:09:14.759
them.

00:09:14.759 --> 00:09:18.389
So Eliade says: that the deluge myth, deluge
myth is almost universally disseminated.

00:09:18.389 --> 00:09:23.509
It is documented in all the continents, although
very rarely in Africa probably because of

00:09:23.509 --> 00:09:25.339
the relative shortage of water.

00:09:25.339 --> 00:09:26.880
And on various cultural levels.

00:09:26.880 --> 00:09:31.490
A certain number of variants seem to be the
result of dissemination, first from Mesopotamia

00:09:31.490 --> 00:09:32.920
and then from India.

00:09:32.920 --> 00:09:38.839
It is equally possible that one or several
diluvial catastrophes gave rise to fabulous

00:09:38.839 --> 00:09:43.319
narratives, but it would be risky to explain
so widespread a myth by phenomena of which

00:09:43.319 --> 00:09:44.723
no geological traces have been found.

00:09:44.723 --> 00:09:49.829
That majority of the flood myths seem in some
sense to form part of the cosmic rhythm.

00:09:49.829 --> 00:09:55.259
The old world, people by a fallen humanity
is submerged under the water and sometime

00:09:55.259 --> 00:09:58.149
later a new world emerges from the aquatic
chaos.

00:09:58.149 --> 00:10:03.470
In a large number of variants the flood is
the result of the sins or ritual faults of

00:10:03.470 --> 00:10:05.080
human beings.

00:10:05.080 --> 00:10:10.500
Sometimes it results simply from the wish
of a divine being to put an end to mankind.

00:10:10.500 --> 00:10:14.279
The chief causes lie at once therefore in
the sins of men and the decrepitude of the

00:10:14.279 --> 00:10:15.279
world.

00:10:15.279 --> 00:10:20.959
by the mere fact that it exists - That is,
that it lives and produces - The cosmos gradually

00:10:20.959 --> 00:10:23.339
deteriorates and ends by falling into decay.

00:10:23.339 --> 00:10:25.889
This is the reason why it has to be recreated.

00:10:25.889 --> 00:10:31.290
In other words, the flood realizes on a macrocosmic
scale what is symbolically affected during

00:10:31.290 --> 00:10:32.500
the New Year festival.

00:10:32.500 --> 00:10:43.460
The end of the world and the end of a sinful
humanity in order to make a new creation possible.

00:10:43.460 --> 00:10:47.970
So then the question might arise logically
enough, what is it that would motivate an

00:10:47.970 --> 00:10:52.480
individual to work to avoid anomaly when it
emerges in his or her own life.

00:10:52.480 --> 00:10:54.630
And to risk an eventual flood.

00:10:54.630 --> 00:11:01.420
And even more profoundly, what would motivate
an individual perhaps to work for the antithesis

00:11:01.420 --> 00:11:06.680
of order, to work to promote the emergence
of chaos, since we know that people are relatively

00:11:06.680 --> 00:11:13.440
ambivalent in their moral stance
Is it possible that we can create a compelling

00:11:13.440 --> 00:11:20.750
motivational story for the desire of the individual
as such to work against the emergence of the

00:11:20.750 --> 00:11:23.730
good rather than for it.

00:11:23.730 --> 00:11:27.009
So let's take a look at what Genesis says
about the creation of experience.

00:11:27.009 --> 00:11:32.080
So first of all, remember we're taking a phenomenological
stance on this story, which is to say that

00:11:32.080 --> 00:11:38.540
this story is not an objective retelling of,
of materialistic emergence.

00:11:38.540 --> 00:11:41.510
It’s something more specifically dramatic.

00:11:41.510 --> 00:11:44.050
It describes the nature of human experience.

00:11:44.050 --> 00:11:45.050
Okay?

00:11:45.050 --> 00:11:46.529
The nature of conscious human experience.

00:11:46.529 --> 00:11:53.199
And in fact the creation story of Genesis
lays explicit stress on individual consciousness

00:11:53.199 --> 00:11:56.740
literally as a precondition for being itself.

00:11:56.740 --> 00:12:01.699
Which is to say that underlying the story
of Genesis is the notion that without whatever

00:12:01.699 --> 00:12:06.810
consciousness is, there would be no segregated
entities and therefore no being.

00:12:06.810 --> 00:12:12.740
So this is one manner in which Genesis attempts
to put human beings at the centre of the cosmos,

00:12:12.740 --> 00:12:18.920
so to speak, which is the idea that the world
independently of consciousness, whatever that

00:12:18.920 --> 00:12:24.959
world is absolutely needs to be reflected
by consciousness in order to exist in any

00:12:24.959 --> 00:12:28.790
sense that existence could reasonably be defined.

00:12:28.790 --> 00:12:33.380
First chapter:
"In the beginning God created the heaven and

00:12:33.380 --> 00:12:34.380
the earth.

00:12:34.380 --> 00:12:35.410
And the earth was without form and void.

00:12:35.410 --> 00:12:37.670
And darkness was on the face of the deep."

00:12:37.670 --> 00:12:42.290
Now, the idea that the earth was without form
and void takes us back to the [13:48:55] Mesopotamian

00:12:42.290 --> 00:12:48.889
creation myth and because the word for void,
the Hebrew word for void is “Tehom”.

00:12:48.889 --> 00:12:52.430
And “Tehom” is a word derived from Timat.

00:12:52.430 --> 00:12:58.660
And the void, the chaos that constitutes the
unformed condition of the cosmos prior to

00:12:58.660 --> 00:13:04.889
the elaboration of being is assimilated to
the same category as Timat, which is this

00:13:04.889 --> 00:13:11.360
terrible unformed and frightening aprioric
condition that has to be courageously confronted

00:13:11.360 --> 00:13:13.570
in order to manifest itself as being.

00:13:13.570 --> 00:13:17.450
"And the earth was without form and void and
darkness was on the face of the deep."

00:13:17.450 --> 00:13:23.310
So now you see another, another interplay
of opposites here between matter and water,

00:13:23.310 --> 00:13:24.620
the primordial elements.

00:13:24.620 --> 00:13:26.300
So first of all it's heaven and earth.

00:13:26.300 --> 00:13:30.420
And then it's earth and water and, and the
height and the deep.

00:13:30.420 --> 00:13:33.620
And the spirit of God moved upon the face
of the water.

00:13:33.620 --> 00:13:39.639
So another opposite: that interaction between
spirit and whatever it is that the precosmogonic

00:13:39.639 --> 00:13:42.000
water or chaos constitutes.

00:13:42.000 --> 00:13:44.779
"And God said let there be light.

00:13:44.779 --> 00:13:45.779
And there was light.

00:13:45.779 --> 00:13:47.420
And God saw the light, that it was good.

00:13:47.420 --> 00:13:49.369
And God divided the light from the darkness.

00:13:49.369 --> 00:13:50.369
"

00:13:50.369 --> 00:13:54.389
And then a prototypical division between light,
which is associated with illumination and

00:13:54.389 --> 00:13:58.779
enlightenment and consciousness because we're
conscious during the day.

00:13:58.779 --> 00:14:07.470
And the sun and life that emerges nested inside
this, the initial opening lines of this sentence.

00:14:07.470 --> 00:14:13.060
Northrop Frye notes that there's tremendous
emphasis on the notion of a repetitive cycling

00:14:13.060 --> 00:14:18.389
of days and nights in the opening sentences
of Genesis, even though from a formal perspective

00:14:18.389 --> 00:14:24.240
this emphasis is paradoxical because the notion
of the day emerges before the creation of

00:14:24.240 --> 00:14:25.240
the sun.

00:14:25.240 --> 00:14:29.560
And Fry's point is not that this is some careless
gesture on the part of the people who authored

00:14:29.560 --> 00:14:30.560
Genesis.

00:14:30.560 --> 00:14:35.480
But more that it's an attempt to emphasize
the idea of a cyclical relationship between

00:14:35.480 --> 00:14:41.620
consciousness and light and darkness and chaos
and to highlight the idea that this cyclical

00:14:41.620 --> 00:14:46.750
relationship is somehow absolutely vital to
being itself.

00:14:46.750 --> 00:14:52.569
So Genesis one five says "and God called the
light day and the darkness he called night.

00:14:52.569 --> 00:14:54.480
And the evening and the morning were the first
day "

00:14:54.480 --> 00:14:59.120
Frye says "... the central metaphor underlying
beginning is not really birth at all.

00:14:59.120 --> 00:15:02.009
It is rather the moment of waking from sleep.

00:15:02.009 --> 00:15:07.990
When one world disappears, a world of virtuality
and potential, and another comes into actual

00:15:07.990 --> 00:15:08.990
being.

00:15:08.990 --> 00:15:10.899
This is still contained within a cycle.

00:15:10.899 --> 00:15:14.459
We know that at the end of the day we shall
return to the world of sleep..."

00:15:14.459 --> 00:15:19.449
and that's a notion that has a metaphorical
resonance because there's the sleep that punctuates

00:15:19.449 --> 00:15:20.449
periods of consciousness.

00:15:20.449 --> 00:15:25.139
And then there's the great sleep at the end
of life, which is characterized by the complete

00:15:25.139 --> 00:15:27.870
cessation of consciousness.

00:15:27.870 --> 00:15:30.990
We know that at the end of the day we shall
return to the world of sleep.

00:15:30.990 --> 00:15:35.889
But in the meantime there's a sense of self-transcendence
of a consciousness getting up from an unreal

00:15:35.889 --> 00:15:38.760
into a real or at least more real world.

00:15:38.760 --> 00:15:43.860
This sense of awakening into a greater degree
of reality is expressed by Haraclitis as a

00:15:43.860 --> 00:15:49.019
passing from a world where everyone has his
own logos, into a world where there's a common

00:15:49.019 --> 00:15:52.160
logos - experience that we all share.

00:15:52.160 --> 00:15:57.589
"Genesis presents the creation as a sudden
coming into being of a world through articulate

00:15:57.589 --> 00:16:04.410
speech, which is another aspect of logos"logos
incorporates the idea of creative exploration,

00:16:04.410 --> 00:16:09.410
And then the formulation of the consequences
of that exploration in verbally communicable

00:16:09.410 --> 00:16:10.730
categories
Right?

00:16:10.730 --> 00:16:16.470
Which give our, give our aspects of our being
their defined boundaries and parameters and

00:16:16.470 --> 00:16:22.350
enable us to establish a shared mode of social
being- through articulate speech conscious

00:16:22.350 --> 00:16:24.540
perception light and stability.

00:16:24.540 --> 00:16:27.730
Something like this metaphor of awakening
may be the real reason for the emphasis on

00:16:27.730 --> 00:16:29.519
days and such recurring phrases.

00:16:29.519 --> 00:16:33.379
"And the evening and the morning were the
first day", even before the day as we know

00:16:33.379 --> 00:16:41.889
it was established with the creating of the
sun

00:16:41.889 --> 00:16:48.110
The most fundamental pair of conflicting and
cyclically interacting pairs of opposites

00:16:48.110 --> 00:16:55.379
that is portrayed in Genesis is essentially
the pairing of chaos versus order, chaos versus

00:16:55.379 --> 00:16:57.040
generative order.

00:16:57.040 --> 00:17:02.149
And a poem by F.I Tiuitchev expresses this
idea extremely well and very powerfully.

00:17:02.149 --> 00:17:03.680
So I'm going to read it to you.

00:17:03.680 --> 00:17:08.720
When sacred night sweeps heavenward she takes
the glad the winsome day.

00:17:08.720 --> 00:17:12.059
Unfolding it,
rolls up it's golden carpet that had been

00:17:12.059 --> 00:17:14.930
spread over an abysmal pit.

00:17:14.930 --> 00:17:17.320
Gone vision like as the external world.

00:17:17.320 --> 00:17:22.370
And man a homeless orphan has to face
in utter helplessness naked, alone

00:17:22.370 --> 00:17:24.670
the blackness of immeasurable space.

00:17:24.670 --> 00:17:31.080
Upon himself he has to lean with mind
abolished, thought unfathered in the dim

00:17:31.080 --> 00:17:33.059
depths of his soul he sinks.

00:17:33.059 --> 00:17:36.160
For nothing comes
from outside to support or limit him.

00:17:36.160 --> 00:17:41.740
All life and brightness seem an ancient dream
while in the substance of the night

00:17:41.740 --> 00:17:47.760
unraveled, alien, he now perceives
a faithful something that is his by right.

00:17:47.760 --> 00:17:51.310
Um, absolutely brilliant poetic statement,
I think.

00:17:51.310 --> 00:17:57.580
Laying out very nicely, very richly the, the
fundamental nature of the existential paradox

00:17:57.580 --> 00:17:59.760
that constitutes human life.

00:17:59.760 --> 00:18:03.910
Pointing to a very profound sense of futility
and fear.

00:18:03.910 --> 00:18:08.860
But then beyond that to the notion that in
the depths of the unknown, in the depths of

00:18:08.860 --> 00:18:14.520
the darkness and in the depths of all that,
that's fundamentally unfaceable, there still

00:18:14.520 --> 00:18:20.910
lurks something that can be discovered given
sufficient courage.

00:18:20.910 --> 00:18:27.500
Another fundamental division portrayed indirectly
in Genesis, the word versus chaos.

00:18:27.500 --> 00:18:32.420
So what you have in genesis is an absolutely
stellar idea.

00:18:32.420 --> 00:18:38.530
I think perhaps the most fundamental contribution
of archaic Jewish thinking to western and

00:18:38.530 --> 00:18:43.660
world civilization, which is that although
it is easier in some ways to consider the

00:18:43.660 --> 00:18:49.930
actual matrix of things, their material substrate
as the strata from which they emerge, it is

00:18:49.930 --> 00:18:57.120
equally reasonable and perhaps more pragmatically
useful to note that things only exist because

00:18:57.120 --> 00:19:01.790
of the interaction between the logos, the
word that characterizes consciousness.

00:19:01.790 --> 00:19:03.440
And whatever this matrix is.

00:19:03.440 --> 00:19:09.040
So in Jewish thought and then Christian thought,
and of course in thoughts of that sort echoed

00:19:09.040 --> 00:19:14.460
throughout the world, there's the idea that
consciousness associated with the transcendent

00:19:14.460 --> 00:19:19.800
directly associated with the deity is actually
the thing that in interaction with this matrix

00:19:19.800 --> 00:19:23.530
give, gives rise to being.

00:19:23.530 --> 00:19:29.370
Genesis plays a stress, places stress on this
notion of the internal logos, the individual

00:19:29.370 --> 00:19:31.790
consciousness in two very complex ways.

00:19:31.790 --> 00:19:38.630
It first says that it's the word of God, the
logos of God that gives, that gives order

00:19:38.630 --> 00:19:40.700
to chaos and makes being emerge.

00:19:40.700 --> 00:19:48.100
But then even more particularly it's the,
it’s the self-conscious logos of individual

00:19:48.100 --> 00:19:51.870
humans, their capacity not just to see the
world as an object.

00:19:51.870 --> 00:19:57.400
But also to see themselves as an object that
gives the world the particular value slant

00:19:57.400 --> 00:19:58.460
that it has for us.

00:19:58.460 --> 00:20:03.940
which is to say that not only are we in a
world where the subject and the object are

00:20:03.940 --> 00:20:04.990
separated.

00:20:04.990 --> 00:20:09.710
And, and therefore experience and suffer the
consequences of that separation-But even more

00:20:09.710 --> 00:20:16.160
particularly we are the only creatures who
are so conscious that we can observe ourself

00:20:16.160 --> 00:20:17.160
as objects.

00:20:17.160 --> 00:20:21.770
And the consequence of that is that because
we've extended our consciousness to ourself,

00:20:21.770 --> 00:20:26.320
we're capable of conceptualizing things that
other creatures cannot conceptualize.

00:20:26.320 --> 00:20:31.610
Such as the infinite possibility that lays
manifest of the unknown but also the fact

00:20:31.610 --> 00:20:37.710
that as individuals we're subject to our finite
limitations, right?

00:20:37.710 --> 00:20:39.380
That we can become diseased.

00:20:39.380 --> 00:20:40.810
That we can become mentally ill.

00:20:40.810 --> 00:20:42.840
And that finally we'll die.

00:20:42.840 --> 00:20:48.470
And so the idea here is that something like
the extension of logos to the object, to the

00:20:48.470 --> 00:20:55.990
subject has made human existence finally problematic.

00:20:55.990 --> 00:21:01.120
And genesis refers to this as essentially
the heritable sin of Adam.

00:21:01.120 --> 00:21:07.410
Because we're aware of our own vulnerability
as a genetic consequence merely of being human.

00:21:07.410 --> 00:21:13.410
There's a transformation in the nature of
experience that has essentially cosmic significance.

00:21:13.410 --> 00:21:24.300
Lao Tzu in the Tao Te Ching makes a comment
on the formless chaos that constitutes the

00:21:24.300 --> 00:21:27.430
matrix of things, the origin of things in
the following manner.

00:21:27.430 --> 00:21:33.390
He says "there was something formless yet
complete that existed before heaven and earth

00:21:33.390 --> 00:21:35.570
without sound, without substance.

00:21:35.570 --> 00:21:37.280
"
This is the void or the chaos.

00:21:37.280 --> 00:21:40.930
"Dependent on nothing, unchanging all pervading.

00:21:40.930 --> 00:21:41.930
Unfailing.

00:21:41.930 --> 00:21:44.500
One may think of it as the mother of all things
under heaven."

00:21:44.500 --> 00:21:51.320
The idea here being that whatever experience
is in the absence of a delimited human consciousness,

00:21:51.320 --> 00:21:54.110
is something that’s outside the boundaries
of time.

00:21:54.110 --> 00:21:56.930
Because time -temporality is a human attribute.

00:21:56.930 --> 00:22:02.030
And it's outside the boundaries of spatial
limitation because only human beings with

00:22:02.030 --> 00:22:08.750
their delimited and fixed size can attribute
spatial aspects to being itself.

00:22:08.750 --> 00:22:15.040
So whatever it is, is that exists without
us, is so comprehensive and so complete and

00:22:15.040 --> 00:22:21.650
transcends temporal dimensions to such a great
degree that it can't be conceptualized as

00:22:21.650 --> 00:22:22.980
being at all.

00:22:22.980 --> 00:22:26.890
It’s something that transcends being to
such a degree that it's not even nameable

00:22:26.890 --> 00:22:32.090
but still exists as "the mother of all things
under heaven".

00:22:32.090 --> 00:22:39.390
Now Genesis formally associates the human
being with logos.

00:22:39.390 --> 00:22:46.370
And this is a determinative move in human
history just as the Mesopotamians first hypothesized

00:22:46.370 --> 00:22:51.900
that their emperor was equivalent to Marduk,
the force that confronted Timat and carved

00:22:51.900 --> 00:22:57.080
her into pieces and made the world, and just
as the Egyptians conceptualized their pharaoh

00:22:57.080 --> 00:23:03.450
as the intermingling between Osiris, the stability
of the state and Horus the exploratory hero.

00:23:03.450 --> 00:23:09.160
And then disseminated that identity down the
aristocratic levels, closer and closer to

00:23:09.160 --> 00:23:11.280
the individual, individual.

00:23:11.280 --> 00:23:18.670
So the ancient Hebrews said, “and God said
let us make man in our image after our likeness.”

00:23:18.670 --> 00:23:25.470
Now, it could be said that the logical derivation
of that statement is that god looks like human

00:23:25.470 --> 00:23:26.470
beings.

00:23:26.470 --> 00:23:28.700
Or conversely that God is an old man with
a beard.

00:23:28.700 --> 00:23:32.320
But it means something I think that's more
sophisticated than that.

00:23:32.320 --> 00:23:38.350
Which is that the central aspect that's associated
with this transcendent deity, the logos, which

00:23:38.350 --> 00:23:43.680
is the thing that gives rise to order as a
consequence of it's confrontation with chaos

00:23:43.680 --> 00:23:47.560
is also the thing that centrally characterizes
human consciousness.

00:23:47.560 --> 00:23:53.470
And so with that there's this transcendent
notion that inside each human being is a spark

00:23:53.470 --> 00:23:55.460
of genuine divinity.

00:23:55.460 --> 00:24:00.500
And it’s the manifestation of that divinity
in human temporal and spatial parameters that

00:24:00.500 --> 00:24:05.170
literally keeps the cosmos generating.

00:24:05.170 --> 00:24:13.270
"So God created his, man in his own image
in the image of God created he, him.

00:24:13.270 --> 00:24:18.260
Male and female created he them and let them
have dominion over the fish of the sea and

00:24:18.260 --> 00:24:22.370
the fowl of the air and over the cattle and
over all the earth and over every creeping

00:24:22.370 --> 00:24:24.170
thing that creepeth upon the earth.

00:24:24.170 --> 00:24:25.170
"

00:24:25.170 --> 00:24:28.620
Now fundamentalist Christians read this as
an injunction, right?

00:24:28.620 --> 00:24:32.650
This is what human beings should do, dominate
all other living things.

00:24:32.650 --> 00:24:36.950
But it's more like a description, which is
that the consequence of the embeddedness of

00:24:36.950 --> 00:24:42.100
this spark of divinity in the individual is
precisely what gave rise to the human ability

00:24:42.100 --> 00:24:43.440
to dominate the planet.

00:24:43.440 --> 00:24:48.250
Which is an ability that at least at the moment
seems fundamentally unparalleled, with no

00:24:48.250 --> 00:24:50.270
limit in sight.

00:24:50.270 --> 00:24:54.450
So it's not an injunction so much as a cold-hearted
description.

00:24:54.450 --> 00:25:01.170
There's a very profound idea underlying the
necessity of the creation of the individual

00:25:01.170 --> 00:25:02.170
human being.

00:25:02.170 --> 00:25:07.070
Here's a line of archaic Jewish speculation
that runs something like this:

00:25:07.070 --> 00:25:14.410
Why is the creation of a limited subject necessary
if God's omniscient and omnipotent and omnipresent?

00:25:14.410 --> 00:25:17.350
Why would he bother creating anything outside
of himself?

00:25:17.350 --> 00:25:20.170
And the line of speculation runs like this.

00:25:20.170 --> 00:25:26.950
The one thing that a being that is complete
in all regards even all hypothetical regards

00:25:26.950 --> 00:25:30.120
lacks by necessity his limitation.

00:25:30.120 --> 00:25:36.150
And as a consequence of that anything that's
absolute is not complete and can't be complete

00:25:36.150 --> 00:25:37.300
without limitation.

00:25:37.300 --> 00:25:40.571
And so there's an emergent idea in Genesis.

00:25:40.571 --> 00:25:45.970
And most notions of the emergence of human
consciousness that the absolute needs the

00:25:45.970 --> 00:25:52.590
reflection point of a delimited being to actually
spring into some kind of defined actuality.

00:25:52.590 --> 00:25:58.190
So that being itself becomes an interplay
between the necessary limitations of the finite

00:25:58.190 --> 00:26:02.390
and the transcendent reality of the absolute.

00:26:02.390 --> 00:26:09.970
And so being is something that emerges because
of the fact as another ancient Jewish tradition

00:26:09.970 --> 00:26:15.160
has it, God and man are in a sense twins,
mutually dependent on one another for their

00:26:15.160 --> 00:26:18.580
defined being.

00:26:18.580 --> 00:26:22.650
From such a perspective, being has the same
nature as a game.

00:26:22.650 --> 00:26:25.170
When you're playing a game you have to play
by rules.

00:26:25.170 --> 00:26:29.480
Which means that there are things that you
can do while playing the game.

00:26:29.480 --> 00:26:30.740
But there are many, many things you can't
do.

00:26:30.740 --> 00:26:34.840
And that the game could not exist without
the limitations.

00:26:34.840 --> 00:26:39.080
Also predicated on the idea that the imposition,
the Nietzschian idea that the imposition of

00:26:39.080 --> 00:26:45.060
limitations on a structure actually gives
rise to the possibility of diverse new forms.

00:26:45.060 --> 00:26:49.500
Which is also a very sophisticated way of
conceptualizing the world.

00:26:49.500 --> 00:26:56.730
So from the perspective of Genesis, the individual
is the locale of the experiential drama.

00:26:56.730 --> 00:27:54.400
And the fact that the individual is limited
is a necessary precondition for being.

